# Browser targets.
#
# The front end is a React 19 SPA served as an ES module, so any browser without
# module support could never run it - the previous "IE 10" entry was a fiction
# that only made PostCSS emit dead fallbacks.
#
# The `fully supports css-cascade-layers` clause is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
# The framework's CSS is wrapped in `@layer framework` (see
# build/postcss-layer-framework.cjs) so the unlayered extensions layer can
# override it without specificity hacks. Lightning CSS - which Vite 8 uses to
# minify - silently strips `@layer` and hoists the rules whenever a target in
# this list lacks support. That inverts the cascade: framework styles start
# beating extension styles again, with no build error to warn you.
#
# Dropping the clause re-admits op_mini, KaiOS and QQ 14.9, none of which can run
# the app. `npm run verify:layers` asserts the layer survived the build.
defaults and fully supports css-cascade-layers
